  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people whose skills match the work. They judge you by fit, proof and honesty.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is matching what you can do to what the role needs.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and what skills do you have interview answer: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can draft answers and mock questions. Routine drafting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Proof, honest self-assessment and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to practise; later, speak from real work.
  </p>

